% A rule the draft drops as a duplicate is charged to the rewrite's limit
% as a rule it keeps is, since it was built before it was found equal to one
% kept.  p's rule is written four times, and the draft keeps one copy.  The
% rewrite reads the query, p's four rules and q's, 2 + 4 + 1 literals, and
% writes the rewritten query, the seed recording q's binding, q$bf's rule
% and all four copies of p's rule, 2 + 0 + 2 + 4: 15 in all.  A limit of 14
% is outgrown at the fourth copy, which the draft would drop, and the
% warning names p/2.

e(a, b).
e(b, c).
f(a, x).

p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
p(X, Y) :- e(X, Y).
q(X, Y) :- f(X, Y).

p(X, Y), q(a, Z)?
